# Metrics

Business collectors (`Counter`, `Histogram`, …) are declared in `metrics/`, one
module per domain (`orders_metrics.py`). Series that read the Starlette
request belong in `prometheus/`, not here.

The composition root constructs each collector class once on
`PrometheusManager.registry` and injects it. A service or client never calls
`Counter(...)` itself and never defaults to the process-wide `REGISTRY`. Tests
pass a private `CollectorRegistry`.

```python
# BAD - the service owns a process-wide series
class OrdersService:
    def __init__(self) -> None:
        self._reads = Counter("orders_reads_total", "…")

    async def get_order(self, order_id: str) -> Order:
        self._reads.inc()
```

```python
# GOOD - injected
class OrdersService:
    def __init__(self, metrics: OrdersMetrics) -> None:
        self._metrics = metrics

    async def get_order(self, order_id: str) -> Order:
        self._metrics.reads_total.inc()

# composition root, once per app
OrdersMetrics(registry=self._prometheus.registry)
```
